[[File:Keris partisan of breaching detail.png|left|150px]]
The '''keris partisan of breaching''' is a one-handed spear requiring 80 [[Attack]] to equip. It is made by attaching the [[Breach of the Scarab]] jewel to the [[keris partisan]], granting an additional 33% accuracy{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1704107285381787952|date=19 September 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107939|archivedate=19 September 2023|quote=[Is the Keris partisan of breaching accuracy bonus against Kalphites/Scabarites 33% or 4/3?] 33%. Do you expect it to make a noticeable difference?}} against all [[Kalphite_(attribute)|kalphites and scabarites]]. Unlike the other three jewelled keris partisans, this partisan retains its passive effect outside the [[Tombs of Amascut]] [[raid]]. It does not possess a [[special attacks|special attack]].

The keris partisan of breaching retains the effects of the [[keris]] and keris partisan, including the 33% bonus damage against [[Kalphite]]s and [[Scabarites]], and the 1/51 chance of puncturing a hole in their exoskeleton that inflicts triple damage. When this special effect occurs, the chatbox will display the message: {{mes|You slip your weapon through a gap in the creature's chitin, landing a vicious blow.}}

As with the keris partisan, weapon poisons cannot be applied to this partisan.

